 {:seon.task/name "roots-page-shows-each-branchs-drift-from-main"
  :seon.task/plan "Owner via root, 2026-11-14: \"make merging boring so it happens more and agents are just always integrating with main.\" The plan's measure is each branch's drift from main, shown on root's page and derived from branch bases, with no stored counter.\n\nWhat exists [M]:\n- seon.db/branch-base: the db at Datahike's merge-base of a branch and main. agent.clj:564 and writer.clj:19/89/360 already call it.\n- The writer answers {:op :branch-db} to the render proc, as the turns tile's ask-turns uses it (seon.render.proc).\n- A render cannot reach other branches. The turns tile works around that the same way, so both read branches through one mechanism. This is the core's \"render reads branches\", with the tile drawing my.root/turns-of's rows: one way, not two.\n\nDrift of branch b:\n- commits: (:max-tx main) - (:max-tx base), the transactions main took since b last synced;\n- age: the txInstant of main's head minus that of base's last transaction. Both are data, and no wall clock is read (docs/clocks.md).\n- Optional later: the datom count (seon.ctx/moved, O(changed)).\n\nRows: one per live branch, from the store's branch list (d/branches), each with its agent or session.\n\nEstimate (lower bound, as arithmetic):\n- On a main move, every branch's drift grows: O(B) row updates, B the live branches (~10-20).\n- A branch's merge-base is k commit-graph steps since it diverged, each a cached commit read: O(B*k) on a main move, with k reset to 0 on each sync.\n- On a commit to branch b, only b's row moves: O(k_b).\n- At B=20 and k<=50: under 1,000 commit reads per main move.\n- A test at 3 branches holds this as :growth :linear in branches, never in history.\n- Simpler: keep each branch's base as the point its last merge-main! or seon_done wrote (:seon.tx/merged), giving O(1) per branch. Measure both and pick by the 90/10 rule.\n\nProof: seon.render-test/roots-page-shows-each-branchs-drift-from-main. Main moves twice, and a branch that never synced reads 2 commits behind; it merges main and reads 0; a sibling branch stays at 2.\n\nOrder: after web's item 4 (deletions onto the core) and W-5. Needs a render that reads branches through the core.\n\nSimpler, found 17:30 [M, writer.clj:353-361]: the writer's :branch-db answer already carries :base (the merge-base db) and :base-t (main's t there). So drift needs no merge-base of its own: commits behind = (:max-tx main) - :base-t, and age = the txInstant gap between them. The branch Store that seon.render.proc/a-branch-head-is-a-store-a-render-derefs keeps holds both. This drops the O(B*k) design above, and the O(1) per-branch alternative too."
  :seon.task/kind :whole
  :seon.task/proofs #{seon.render-test/roots-page-shows-each-branchs-drift-from-main}
  :seon.task/needs #{"seon.render.proc/a-branch-head-is-a-store-a-render-derefs"}}]
